MAME drawshm, ported to mame0276 for the domainos station.

WHY A SEPARATE VARIANT. See mame-ctlsock-0276.patch's header -- same story,
same station, same tag pin (docs/lab/DOMAINOS-WAVE.md "wall 1": 0.289 cannot
boot the Apollo DN3500 in Normal mode; the station binary is built from
mame0276 instead of the fleet's mame0289).

WHAT DIFFERS FROM mame-drawshm.patch (0289)
  - scripts/src/osd/modules.lua and osdobj_common.cpp: same insertions
    (drawshm.cpp in the file list; RENDERER_SHM registered right after
    RENDERER_NONE), only the surrounding context lines differ.
  - src/osd/modules/render/drawshm.cpp: the seqlock word is flipped from
    C++20 std::atomic_ref onto plain GCC atomic intrinsics
    (__atomic_load_n/__atomic_store_n on the raw uint64_t*), because 0.276's
    own build (REGENIE=1, no C++20 flag) compiles as C++17, where
    std::atomic_ref does not exist. Same memory orders (relaxed load,
    release stores), same seqlock protocol, same wire format -- only the
    atomic primitive changed. MEASURED 2026-09-09 against the working
    0.276 tree (docs/lab/DOMAINOS-WAVE.md wall 1).

